Subject: meson: select UWP from the host machine subsystem

mesa-uwp 34732bb reads get_option('uwp'), a builtin option of an unpublished
Meson fork. The published UWP Meson fork (SternXD/meson uwp-subsystem)
models UWP as a host machine subsystem instead, set in a machine file:

  [host_machine]
  system = 'windows'
  subsystem = 'uwp'

That fork also adds /DWINAPI_FAMILY=WINAPI_FAMILY_APP and the AppContainer
project settings, so with_uwp follows the machine file. Build-only change.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -114,7 +114,9 @@
 with_vulkan_vram_report_limit_layer = get_option('vulkan-layers').contains('vram-report-limit')
 with_vulkan_anti_lag_layer = get_option('vulkan-layers').contains('anti-lag')
 with_tools = get_option('tools')
-with_uwp = get_option('uwp')
+# The UWP Meson fork selects an AppContainer build from the host machine file
+# (system = 'windows', subsystem = 'uwp') rather than a builtin option.
+with_uwp = host_machine.system() == 'windows' and host_machine.subsystem() == 'uwp'
 if with_tools.contains('all')
   with_tools = [
     'amd',
